---
/**
 * FanIntro.astro — the cloud-burst arrival for `/fan/`.
 *
 * ⚠️ **2026-09-30: this is a port of a standalone canvas demo the visitor supplied
 * ("云上旅梦 · Opening Animation"), replacing the CSS-keyframe version.** The demo's
 * technique is kept 1:1 — a low-resolution offscreen canvas of ~200 blurred puffs,
 * composited with `ctx.filter = blur()`, then a hole punched through it with
 * `globalCompositeOperation = "destination-out"` plus sixteen rotating "petals" so
 * the rim is torn rather than circular — and so are its clock and its reveal
 * choreography:
 *
 *   0.12 s   the puffs start rising from below the fold (0.95-1.4 s each, staggered)
 *   1.90 s   the hole starts to open (1.60 s, ease-in-out)
 *   2.35 s   the page's hero starts to arrive: opacity 0 → 1 and a 28px rise, 0.95 s
 *            each, staggered 0 / 0.09 / 0.19 / 0.29 / 0.39 / 0.49 s
 *   3.50 s   the canvas is dropped and the overlay is removed
 *
 * ⚠️ Three adaptations, each for a reason the demo did not have to solve:
 *
 *  1. **The canvas IS the cover, background included.** In the demo the pink field is
 *     a DOM layer UNDER the canvas, because what it covered was the demo's own pink
 *     page. Here the overlay sits on top of the real page, so anything left in the
 *     DOM under the canvas would still be in front of the page after the hole opens.
 *     The field (one linear gradient + three elliptical radials + the masked white
 *     dot texture) is therefore painted INTO the canvas — once, on resize — and the
 *     hole erases the whole thing in a single operation.
 *  2. **The reveal target is the page's own hero, not a duplicated title card.** The
 *     demo's `.content > *` block IS its page. Copying that block's copy into this
 *     overlay would have put two wordmarks on screen a few pixels apart for the
 *     whole second half of the shot; instead the page's hero children start hidden
 *     while `html.is-fi` is set and are released by `html.is-fi-revealed` with the
 *     demo's own stagger. Same choreography, no second copy of anything.
 *  3. **The demo's buttons and chips are not ported.** They are a landing page's CTAs
 *     (「开始探索」/「了解更多」/「治愈系 · 插画集 · 云朵旅」); this hero has no CTAs by
 *     the visitor's own call, and the hero's stamp pill and scroll hint already fill
 *     those two slots.
 *
 * ⚠️ WHEN it plays is a runtime decision made in the script at the bottom: first
 * `/fan/` of the session, or an arrival from any `/art` page. Back/forward never
 * replays it, and reduced motion never gets it at all.
 *
 * ⚠️ The overlay ships VISIBLE in the markup and is taken away when it must not
 * play. The other order — hidden until a script arms it — shows the page first,
 * which is the flash this component exists to avoid.
 *
 * ⚠️ It is a SIBLING of `.fan-root` and the FIRST thing in the page's slot. As a
 * child, `.fan-root > *:not(...)` would force `position: relative` on it; as the
 * first node, the cover is parsed and painted before the page behind it.
 *
 * ⚠️ `html[data-own-intro]` comes from `Layout.astro`'s `ownIntro` prop and makes the
 * site's inline guard stand down. Two consequences relied on: the site cover is never
 * shown here, and `main`'s `pageIn` entrance is switched off below.
 */
import type { Language } from "../utils/i18n";

interface Props {
  /** the route's own language; `/nl/fan/` is served from the same component */
  language?: Language;
}

/* ⚠️ The prop is declared so FanPage can pass it, and deliberately unused: this
   component draws no text of its own any more. The reveal lands on the page's own
   hero, so the copy still comes from src/utils/fan.ts through FanPage. */
---

<div class="fi" id="fan-intro" aria-hidden="true">
  <canvas class="fi-canvas" data-fi-canvas></canvas>
</div>

<noscript>
  <style is:global>
    /* No script, no arrival: the cover would otherwise stay up forever. */
    .fi {
      display: none !important;
    }
  </style>
</noscript>

<style is:global>
  /* ⚠️ `global.css` animates `main` in (`pageIn`: opacity 0 → 1 with a 10px rise).
     On this page the arrival IS the entrance, and pageIn would do two bad things:
     fade the cover in from nothing, and — for the length of the animation — give
     `main` a transform, which turns every `position: fixed` descendant into an
     absolutely positioned one. The cover has to be there on the first painted frame,
     so the site's page entrance stands down here. */
  html[data-own-intro] main {
    animation: none;
  }

  /* ⚠️ Belt and braces: if the arrival's script never runs, the cover must not be
     able to trap a visitor. */
  html:not([data-own-intro]) .fi {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .fi {
      display: none !important;
    }
  }

  /* ══════════ THE REVEAL ══════════
     The demo's `.content > *` rules, pointed at the page's real hero. `is-fi` is set
     by the arrival's script, which runs before the hero is parsed — so the hero is
     never painted in its "arrived" state and then snapped away. */
  html.is-fi:not(.is-fi-revealed) .fan-hero > .hero-blob,
  html.is-fi:not(.is-fi-revealed) .fan-hero > .fan-title,
  html.is-fi:not(.is-fi-revealed) .fan-hero > .fan-title-cn,
  html.is-fi:not(.is-fi-revealed) .fan-hero > .fan-sub,
  html.is-fi:not(.is-fi-revealed) .fan-hero > .fan-stamp {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(28px) scale(0.96);
  }

  /* ⚠️ Armed on the PAGE, not on `is-fi`: the classes are dropped at 3.5s while the
     last staggered item (delay 0.49s + 0.95s) is still moving, and a transition
     declared under `html.is-fi` disappears with it — the hero's stamp and scroll hint
     snapped instead of arriving. */
  html[data-own-intro] .fan-hero > .hero-blob,
  html[data-own-intro] .fan-hero > .fan-title,
  html[data-own-intro] .fan-hero > .fan-title-cn,
  html[data-own-intro] .fan-hero > .fan-sub,
  html[data-own-intro] .fan-hero > .fan-stamp {
    transition:
      opacity 0.95s var(--ease-out),
      transform 0.95s var(--ease-out);
  }

  /* the demo's stagger, in the hero's own reading order */
  html.is-fi-revealed .fan-hero > .hero-blob {
    transition-delay: 0s;
  }
  html.is-fi-revealed .fan-hero > .fan-title {
    transition-delay: 0.09s;
  }
  html.is-fi-revealed .fan-hero > .fan-title-cn {
    transition-delay: 0.19s;
  }
  html.is-fi-revealed .fan-hero > .fan-sub {
    transition-delay: 0.29s;
  }
  html.is-fi-revealed .fan-hero > .fan-stamp {
    transition-delay: 0.39s;
  }

  /* while the arrival plays the page behind it must not scroll */
  html.is-fi {
    overflow: hidden;
  }
</style>

<style>
  /* ⚠️ No background on the overlay itself: the CANVAS is the cover, and anything
     painted here would stay in front of the page once the hole has opened. The one
     exception is the field colour as a first-paint fallback, which the first canvas
     frame replaces within a frame or two. */
  .fi {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100vh;
    height: 100svh;
    /* above the page's own rail and lightbox (9000 / 9500) */
    z-index: 9999;
    overflow: hidden;
    pointer-events: auto;
    /* ⚠️ NO background here, not even as a first-paint fallback — that fallback was
       the bug in the first port of this: the hole erases the CANVAS, so a colour on
       this element stayed behind as a pink wall exactly where the page should have
       been showing. The canvas is painted once synchronously before the first frame
       (`render(0)` below), so there is nothing to cover. */
  }

  /* the last 0.3s: the cover is already fully erased, this only keeps a layer over
     the page while the compositor catches up (see the teardown comment) */
  .fi.is-out {
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.3s linear;
  }

  /* ⚠️ `inset: 0` would not do: during `pageIn` a fixed child resolves against
     `main`, which is the height of the whole page. */
  .fi-canvas {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    display: block;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  /* ⚠️ is:inline, and it has to be. The FIRST thing this script does is put is-fi
     on html, which is what holds the hero's children at opacity 0 — and an Astro
     module script is deferred, i.e. it runs after the document has been parsed,
     which is late enough for the hero to be painted in full and then snapped away.
     Inline means it runs here, before the hero markup exists. Nothing in this block
     is TypeScript, for the same reason. */
  /**
   * The arrival. The canvas work (field, puffs, blur, hole, petals) is ported from
   * the visitor's demo; the trigger rules, the mosaic pause and the teardown are this
   * repo's.
   *
   * ⚠️ The reveal and the teardown ride the LOOP's clock, not `setTimeout` deadlines:
   * the hero has to arrive on the same second as the hole, and a timer that fires
   * 400ms late under load would open the hole ahead of the page.
   */
  (() => {
    const el = document.getElementById("fan-intro");
    const canvas = document.querySelector("[data-fi-canvas]");
    if (!el || !canvas) return;
    const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
    if (!ctx) return;

    const root = document.documentElement;
    const KEY = "rrsuika-fan-intro-seen";

    /** the mosaic's own handle (`FanMosaic.astro` publishes it for A/B probes) */
    /* ⚠️ `FanMosaic` is rendered INSIDE `.fan-root`, i.e. AFTER this component, and
       its script is a deferred module — so at this point its handle does not exist
       yet and a single `pause()` here would silently do nothing (measured: the
       background kept running through the whole arrival). The loop below picks it up
       on the first frame after it appears, which is still behind an opaque cover. */
    let mosaicHeld = false;
    let mosaicBack = false;
    function holdMosaic() {
      if (mosaicHeld || mosaicBack) return;
      const m = window.__fanMosaic;
      if (!m) return;
      m.pause();
      mosaicHeld = true;
    }
    function releaseMosaic() {
      if (mosaicBack) return;
      const m = window.__fanMosaic;
      if (!m) return;
      m.resume();
      mosaicBack = true;
    }

    const TAU = Math.PI * 2;
    const lerp = (a, b, t) => a + (b - a) * t;
    const clamp = (v, a, b) => (v < a ? a : v > b ? b : v);
    const easeOutCubic = (t) => 1 - Math.pow(1 - t, 3);
    const easeInOutCubic = (t) =>
      t < 0.5 ? 4 * t * t * t : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * t + 2, 3) / 2;

    /* ── the demo's clock, unchanged ── */
    const T_RISE = 0.12;
    const T_CRACK_START = 1.9;
    const T_CRACK_DUR = 1.6;
    const T_REVEAL = 2.35;
    const T_TOTAL = T_CRACK_START + T_CRACK_DUR;
    /* ⚠️ The background has to be running again BEFORE the hole exposes it. A paused
       WebGL canvas has no valid drawing buffer left to hand the compositor
       (`preserveDrawingBuffer` is false), so the first frame the visitor sees of it
       after a pause can composite as BLACK — measured with `输入/_scratch/fi-black.mjs`,
       which screencasts the whole arrival and averages every frame. It goes back up
       0.1s before the crack. */
    const T_MOSAIC_BACK = T_CRACK_START - 0.1;

    /* ── the demo's palette ── */
    const C_FIELD_A = "#FFEAF6";
    const C_FIELD_B = "#FFCBE4";
    const C_FIELD_C = "#FFAFD5";
    const C_PUFF_TOP = "#FFFFFF";
    const C_PUFF_BOTTOM = "#FFD1E9";

    /* one puff: {x, y, r, yStart, delay, dur, color, phase}
       one petal: {ang, dist, rad, spin} */

    let W = 0;
    let H = 0;
    let DPR = 1;
    let SCALE = 0.6;
    let blurPx = 14;
    let puffs = [];
    let petals = [];
    let startTime = 0;
    let rafId = 0;
    let revealed = false;
    let finished = false;

    /* the low-resolution puff buffer: one blur per frame, not one per puff */
    const tmp = document.createElement("canvas");
    const tctx = tmp.getContext("2d");
    /* the static cover (field + dots), repainted only on resize */
    const field = document.createElement("canvas");
    const fctx = field.getContext("2d");

    /* Safari < 16.4 has no `ctx.filter`; the demo's radial-gradient fallback stays */
    const supportsFilter = (() => {
      try {
        const c = document.createElement("canvas").getContext("2d");
        if (!c) return false;
        c.filter = "blur(2px)";
        return c.filter === "blur(2px)";
      } catch (_) {
        return false;
      }
    })();

    const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;

    function mixHex(a, b, t) {
      const pa = [
        parseInt(a.slice(1, 3), 16),
        parseInt(a.slice(3, 5), 16),
        parseInt(a.slice(5, 7), 16),
      ];
      const pb = [
        parseInt(b.slice(1, 3), 16),
        parseInt(b.slice(3, 5), 16),
        parseInt(b.slice(5, 7), 16),
      ];
      return `rgb(${Math.round(lerp(pa[0], pb[0], t))},${Math.round(
        lerp(pa[1], pb[1], t),
      )},${Math.round(lerp(pa[2], pb[2], t))})`;
    }

    /* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       THE COVER (the demo's `.bg`, painted instead of styled)

       ⚠️ Canvas radial gradients are CIRCLES; the demo's are ellipses. Each one is
       drawn inside `translate + scale`, which is the standard way to get an
       elliptical gradient out of the 2D context; the fill rect is expressed in the
       scaled space so it covers the whole ellipse.
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
    function paintField() {
      if (!fctx) return;
      const w = Math.max(1, Math.round(W * DPR));
      const h = Math.max(1, Math.round(H * DPR));
      field.width = w;
      field.height = h;
      fctx.setTransform(DPR, 0, 0, DPR, 0, 0);

      /* linear-gradient(168deg, #FFEAF6 0%, #FFCBE4 48%, #FFAFD5 100%) */
      const ang = ((168 - 90) * Math.PI) / 180;
      const dx = Math.cos(ang);
      const dy = Math.sin(ang);
      const len = Math.abs(W * dx) + Math.abs(H * dy);
      const g = fctx.createLinearGradient(
        W / 2 - (dx * len) / 2,
        H / 2 - (dy * len) / 2,
        W / 2 + (dx * len) / 2,
        H / 2 + (dy * len) / 2,
      );
      g.addColorStop(0, C_FIELD_A);
      g.addColorStop(0.48, C_FIELD_B);
      g.addColorStop(1, C_FIELD_C);
      fctx.fillStyle = g;
      fctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

      const ellipse = (cx, cy, rx, ry, color, stop) => {
        fctx.save();
        fctx.translate(cx, cy);
        fctx.scale(rx, ry);
        const rg = fctx.createRadialGradient(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1);
        rg.addColorStop(0, color);
        rg.addColorStop(stop, "rgba(255,255,255,0)");
        fctx.fillStyle = rg;
        fctx.fillRect(-2, -2, 4, 4);
        fctx.restore();
      };

      /* the three radials, bottom layer first (CSS paints that list in reverse) */
      ellipse(W * 0.92, H * 0.22, W * 0.75, H * 0.65, "#FFE2F1", 0.62);
      ellipse(W * 0.12, H * 0.08, W * 0.85, H * 0.75, "#FFFFFF", 0.58);
      ellipse(W * 0.5, H * 1.12, W * 1.2, H * 0.95, "#FF9BC6", 0.62);

      /* ── the dot texture, on its own layer so its mask cannot erase the field ──
         `.bg::after`: 1.5px white dots on a 36px pitch at 0.32, faded out in the
         middle by `radial-gradient(circle at 50% 45%, transparent 18%, #000 78%)`. */
      const dots = document.createElement("canvas");
      dots.width = w;
      dots.height = h;
      const dctx = dots.getContext("2d");
      if (!dctx) return;
      dctx.setTransform(DPR, 0, 0, DPR, 0, 0);
      dctx.fillStyle = "#FFFFFF";
      for (let y = 18; y < H; y += 36) {
        for (let x = 18; x < W; x += 36) {
          dctx.beginPath();
          dctx.arc(x, y, 1.5, 0, TAU);
          dctx.fill();
        }
      }
      dctx.globalCompositeOperation = "destination-in";
      const far = Math.hypot(W * 0.5, H * 0.55);
      const mk = dctx.createRadialGradient(W * 0.5, H * 0.45, 0, W * 0.5, H * 0.45, far);
      mk.addColorStop(0, "rgba(0,0,0,0)");
      mk.addColorStop(0.18, "rgba(0,0,0,0)");
      mk.addColorStop(0.78, "rgba(0,0,0,1)");
      dctx.fillStyle = mk;
      dctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
      fctx.globalAlpha = 0.32;
      fctx.drawImage(dots, 0, 0, W, H);
      fctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    }

    /* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       CLOUDS
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
    function buildClouds() {
      puffs = [];
      const base = Math.min(W, H);
      const spacing = clamp(base * 0.135, 56, 130);
      const cols = Math.ceil(W / spacing) + 5;
      const rows = Math.ceil(H / spacing) + 5;
      const offX = -spacing * 2.5;
      const offY = -spacing * 2.5;

      for (let r = 0; r < rows; r++) {
        for (let c = 0; c < cols; c++) {
          const jx = (Math.random() - 0.5) * spacing * 0.72;
          const jy = (Math.random() - 0.5) * spacing * 0.72;
          const x = offX + c * spacing + jx;
          const y = offY + r * spacing + jy;
          const rad = spacing * (0.86 + Math.random() * 0.46);
          /* lower puffs are pinker: that gradient is what reads as volume */
          const k = clamp(y / H, 0, 1);
          puffs.push({
            x,
            y,
            r: rad,
            yStart: H + rad + 40 + Math.random() * H * 0.45,
            delay: T_RISE + Math.random() * 0.34,
            dur: 0.95 + Math.random() * 0.45,
            color: mixHex(C_PUFF_TOP, C_PUFF_BOTTOM, k * 0.9),
            phase: Math.random() * TAU,
          });
        }
      }
    }

    function buildPetals() {
      petals = [];
      const N = 16;
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        petals.push({
          ang: (i / N) * TAU + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.38,
          dist: 0.62 + Math.random() * 0.44,
          rad: 0.34 + Math.random() * 0.3,
          spin: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 1.7,
        });
      }
    }

    function resize() {
      W = window.innerWidth;
      H = window.innerHeight;
      DPR = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
      canvas.width = Math.round(W * DPR);
      canvas.height = Math.round(H * DPR);
      canvas.style.width = W + "px";
      canvas.style.height = H + "px";
      ctx.setTransform(DPR, 0, 0, DPR, 0, 0);

      /* a fixed pixel budget for the puff buffer, so the blur costs the same on a
         phone and on a 4K monitor */
      SCALE = clamp(Math.sqrt(850000 / Math.max(W * H, 1)), 0.34, 0.66);
      tmp.width = Math.max(1, Math.round(W * SCALE));
      tmp.height = Math.max(1, Math.round(H * SCALE));
      blurPx = clamp(Math.min(W, H) * 0.028, 8, 26);

      paintField();
      buildClouds();
      buildPetals();
    }

    function drawCloudLayer(t) {
      if (!tctx) return;
      const tw = tmp.width;
      const th = tmp.height;
      tctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);
      tctx.clearRect(0, 0, tw, th);
      tctx.setTransform(SCALE, 0, 0, SCALE, 0, 0);

      for (let i = 0; i < puffs.length; i++) {
        const p = puffs[i];
        const prog = clamp((t - p.delay) / p.dur, 0, 1);
        if (prog <= 0) continue;
        const e = easeOutCubic(prog);
        const y = lerp(p.yStart, p.y, e);
        if (y - p.r > H + 80) continue;
        if (y + p.r < -80) continue;
        const x = p.x + Math.sin(t * 1.1 + p.phase) * 5 * e;

        if (supportsFilter) {
          tctx.fillStyle = p.color;
          tctx.beginPath();
          tctx.arc(x, y, p.r, 0, TAU);
          tctx.fill();
        } else {
          const rg = tctx.createRadialGradient(x, y, p.r * 0.15, x, y, p.r * 1.1);
          rg.addColorStop(0, p.color);
          rg.addColorStop(0.6, p.color);
          rg.addColorStop(1, "rgba(255,255,255,0)");
          tctx.fillStyle = rg;
          tctx.beginPath();
          tctx.arc(x, y, p.r * 1.1, 0, TAU);
          tctx.fill();
        }
      }
      ctx.save();
      if (supportsFilter) ctx.filter = "blur(" + blurPx + "px)";
      ctx.drawImage(tmp, 0, 0, tw, th, 0, 0, W, H);
      ctx.restore();
    }

    /** the hole: a soft disc plus sixteen rotating petals, so the rim is torn */
    function punchHole(p, t) {
      if (p <= 0) return;
      const cx = W * 0.5;
      const cy = H * 0.5;
      const maxR = Math.hypot(W, H) * 0.63;
      const R = easeInOutCubic(p) * maxR;
      if (R < 0.5) return;

      ctx.save();
      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = "destination-out";

      const g = ctx.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, R * 0.42, cx, cy, R * 1.03);
      g.addColorStop(0, "rgba(0,0,0,1)");
      g.addColorStop(0.6, "rgba(0,0,0,1)");
      g.addColorStop(1, "rgba(0,0,0,0)");
      ctx.fillStyle = g;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(cx, cy, R * 1.03, 0, TAU);
      ctx.fill();

      for (let i = 0; i < petals.length; i++) {
        const pt = petals[i];
        const ang = pt.ang + t * 0.28 * pt.spin;
        const d = R * pt.dist;
        const px = cx + Math.cos(ang) * d;
        const py = cy + Math.sin(ang) * d;
        const pr = R * pt.rad;
        if (pr < 2) continue;
        const pg = ctx.createRadialGradient(px, py, pr * 0.22, px, py, pr);
        pg.addColorStop(0, "rgba(0,0,0,1)");
        pg.addColorStop(0.52, "rgba(0,0,0,1)");
        pg.addColorStop(1, "rgba(0,0,0,0)");
        ctx.fillStyle = pg;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(px, py, pr, 0, TAU);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      ctx.restore();
    }

    function render(t) {
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
      ctx.drawImage(field, 0, 0, W, H);
      drawCloudLayer(t);
      punchHole(clamp((t - T_CRACK_START) / T_CRACK_DUR, 0, 1), t);
    }

    /* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       THE CLOCK
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
    function frame(now) {
      /* ⚠️ A frame can already be in flight when `__fanIntro.step()` cancels the loop;
         without this guard that frame renders the LIVE clock over the frozen one and,
         past 3.5s, tears the whole arrival down under the probe. */
      if (finished) return;
      if (!startTime) startTime = now;
      const t = (now - startTime) / 1000;
      render(t);

      holdMosaic();
      if (mosaicHeld && t >= T_MOSAIC_BACK) releaseMosaic();
      if (!revealed && t >= T_REVEAL) {
        revealed = true;
        root.classList.add("is-fi-revealed");
      }
      if (t >= T_TOTAL) {
        finish();
        return;
      }
      rafId = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    function finish() {
      if (finished) return;
      finished = true;
      cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
      /* ⚠️ `is-fi` goes at the same moment as the overlay: it is what holds the
         hero's children at opacity 0, so leaving it behind would hide the page. */
      root.classList.remove("is-fi", "is-fi-revealed");
      releaseMosaic();
      /* ⚠️ NOT `el.remove()` in this frame. Deleting a full-screen layer in one go
         makes the compositor show the freshly exposed page before it has been
         rasterised, and the visitor sees a black frame between the clouds and the
         interface (「云朵四散的时候，画面会突然变黑，然后才是亮色的界面」; measured as
         one frame at mean luminance 43 out of 255). Fading the last of the cover out
         gives the page underneath those frames. */
      el.classList.add("is-out");
      window.setTimeout(() => el.remove(), 320);
    }

    /* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SHOULD IT PLAY?
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
    let seen = false;
    try {
      seen = sessionStorage.getItem(KEY) === "1";
    } catch (_) {}

    let type = "navigate";
    try {
      const entry = performance.getEntriesByType("navigation")[0];
      type = (entry && entry.type) || "navigate";
    } catch (_) {}

    /* Arriving from the art pages is an explicit "show me the fan page" move, so it
       replays the arrival even inside the same session. Anything else plays once, and
       a back/forward never does. */
    let fromArt = false;
    try {
      fromArt = /\/art(\/|\?|$)/.test(document.referrer);
    } catch (_) {}

    if (reduceMotion || type === "back_forward" || (!fromArt && seen)) {
      el.remove();
      return;
    }

    try {
      sessionStorage.setItem(KEY, "1");
    } catch (_) {}

    /* ⚠️ Set BEFORE the hero markup is parsed (this script is the first thing in the
       page's slot), so the hero is never painted and then hidden. */
    root.classList.add("is-fi");
    holdMosaic();

    resize();
    /* ⚠️ One synchronous frame before the loop starts: the canvas has to be opaque on
       the very first painted frame, or the page shows through it for one frame. */
    render(0);
    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(frame);

    /* the safety net: a canvas that never ran must not leave a cover — or a hidden
       hero — behind it */
    window.setTimeout(() => {
      if (!document.getElementById("fan-intro")) return;
      canvas.style.display = "none";
      finish();
    }, 8000);

    /* ⚠️ A debug hook, like the demo's own `window.__cloudIntro`: `step(t)` stops the
       loop and draws ONE frame at `t` seconds. It exists because a screenshot of this
       page costs longer than the crack itself (measured 0.3-1.7s), so the only honest
       way to photograph the middle of it is to hold the clock still — which is what
       `输入/_scratch/fi-look.mjs` does. `resume()` puts the loop back. */
    window.__fanIntro = {
      info() {
        return { playing: !finished, revealed, t: startTime ? (performance.now() - startTime) / 1000 : 0 };
      },
      step(seconds) {
        finished = true;
        cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
        render(seconds);
      },
      resume() {
        if (!finished) return;
        finished = false;
        startTime = 0;
        root.classList.remove("is-fi-revealed");
        rafId = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
      },
    };

    /* ⚠️ The demo's resize handler, kept as it was: rebuilding the puff field at the
       start is invisible, rebuilding it mid-rise would snap every cloud back to the
       floor, so a later resize only re-seats the ones that have already landed. */
    let resizeTimer = 0;
    window.addEventListener(
      "resize",
      () => {
        if (finished) return;
        window.clearTimeout(resizeTimer);
        resizeTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
          const elapsed = startTime ? (performance.now() - startTime) / 1000 : 0;
          resize();
          if (elapsed >= 0.15) {
            for (let i = 0; i < puffs.length; i++) {
              const p = puffs[i];
              if (elapsed > p.delay + p.dur) p.yStart = p.y;
            }
          }
        }, 180);
      },
      { passive: true },
    );
  })();
</script>
